{%- import "macros.njk" as m with context -%}
{%- set latest = history.years[history.years.length - 1] -%}
{%- set before = history.years[history.years.length - 2] -%}
<h1>Triple lock calculator</h1>

<p class="lede">How the yearly increase is chosen and applied: for any past decision, or for figures you choose. The rule itself is explained on <a href="/triple-lock/">the triple lock</a>. <a href="/tools/">All tools</a>.</p>

<section class="tool" aria-labelledby="tool">
  <h2 id="tool">Try the triple lock</h2>

  <p>This tool shows how the increase is chosen and applied. It works on <strong>one part</strong> of the State Pension: a full rate that follows the triple lock. Other parts of a payment can rise by a different rule.</p>
  <p>All amounts are weekly and before tax. They are not your entitlement: for that, <a href="https://www.gov.uk/check-state-pension">check your State Pension forecast</a> on GOV.UK.</p>
  {#- Shown only once the form is, so a reader without it is not told what to type (W39). -#}
  <p class="js-only">Do not enter your whole pension payment. The tool does not send or store anything you enter, and puts nothing in the page address on its own; a link you copy holds the figures shown. <a href="/privacy/#tools">Privacy</a>.</p>

  <div class="no-js-only">
    {% call m.note("The calculator needs JavaScript", 3, "the-calculator-needs-javascript") %}
    <p>The calculator is not available, because JavaScript is off or did not load. <span class="if-script-failed">The script for this form did not run to the end, though the page's other scripts did. Reload the page; if that does not help, <a href="/sources-and-method/#report-an-error">report it</a>.</span> The <a href="/triple-lock/#worked-example">worked example on the triple lock page</a> and the table of <a href="/history/#decisions">every decision since 2010</a> show the same method.</p>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>

  <div class="tool-layout">
  <form id="mechanism-form" class="js-only" novalidate>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>Start from a past decision</legend>
      <div class="fields">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="mechanism-year">Tax year</label>
          <select id="mechanism-year" name="mechanism-year">
            {%- for year in history.years | reverse %}{% if year.measure != "pre-triple-lock" %}
            <option value="{{ year.tax_year }}">{{ year.tax_year }}</option>
            {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="mechanism-series">Pension</label>
          <select id="mechanism-series" name="mechanism-series">
            <option value="new">Full new State Pension</option>
            <option value="basic">Full basic State Pension</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="secondary" id="mechanism-load">Load this decision</button>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset id="mechanism-figures">
      <legend>Figures used</legend>
      <p>Showing: <span class="tool-mode" id="mechanism-mode">Past decision: {{ latest.tax_year }}, as published</span></p>
      <p>Change any figure and the result follows it, labelled hypothetical.</p>
      <div class="fields">
        {{ m.field("mechanism-prices", "Rise in prices", latest.prices_tenths | plainPercent, "Per cent, from -10 to 25. One decimal place.", "", "%") }}
        {{ m.field("mechanism-earnings", "Rise in earnings", latest.earnings_tenths | plainPercent, "Per cent, from -10 to 25. One decimal place.", "", "%") }}
        {{ m.field("mechanism-start", "Weekly amount before the increase", before.new_pence | plainPounds, "A full rate, in pounds. From 1 to 1,000.", "£", "") }}
      </div>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="buttons">
      <button type="button" class="secondary" id="mechanism-copy-link" aria-describedby="mechanism-copy-hint">Copy a link to this result</button>
    </div>
    {% set mechanism_copy_hint %}The link holds the year and pension chosen and the three figures shown, including any you typed. Copying a link does not change the page address; only if the link cannot be copied is it put there for you to copy.{% endset %}
    <p class="hint" aria-hidden="true">{{ mechanism_copy_hint }}</p>
    <span id="mechanism-copy-hint" hidden>{{ mechanism_copy_hint }}</span>
    <p class="hint" id="mechanism-copy-note" aria-hidden="true"></p>
  </form>
  <div class="tool-summary js-only">
    <h3 id="mechanism-glance-heading">At a glance</h3>
    <div id="mechanism-glance">
      <p>The result appears here as you fill in the form.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>

  <p class="visually-hidden" role="status" id="mechanism-status"></p>

  <div class="result" id="mechanism-result">
    <h3 id="mechanism-result-heading">Full new State Pension, {{ latest.tax_year }}: what was decided</h3>
    <p class="headline">{{ latest.applied_tenths | percent }} increase, decided by earnings</p>
    <dl>
      <dt>Prices, year to the September before</dt> <dd>{{ latest.prices_tenths | percent }}</dd>
      <dt>Earnings, May to July before, as published at the time</dt> <dd>{{ latest.earnings_tenths | percent }}</dd>
      <dt>Minimum</dt> <dd>2.5%</dd>
      <dt>Weekly rate before</dt> <dd>{{ before.new_pence | money }}</dd>
      <dt>Weekly rate after, as published</dt> <dd>{{ latest.new_pence | money }}</dd>
      <dt>Weekly increase</dt> <dd>{{ (latest.new_pence - before.new_pence) | money }}</dd>
      <dt>52 weeks at the new rate</dt> <dd>{{ (latest.new_pence * 52) | money }}</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>These are the published decision and the published rates. This tool did not calculate them.</p>
    <p class="source-line">{% if latest.rate_source_url == latest.decision_source_url %}Source: <a href="{{ latest.decision_source_url }}">the explanatory memorandum to the Up-rating Order for {{ latest.tax_year }}</a>{% else %}Sources: <a href="{{ latest.rate_source_url }}">the published rates for {{ latest.tax_year }}</a> and <a href="{{ latest.decision_source_url }}">the explanatory memorandum to the Up-rating Order</a>{% endif %}, as recorded on <a href="/history/#decisions">the history page</a>. Checked against the sources on {{ history.checked_date | dateText }}.</p>
  </div>

  <h3 id="how-the-tool-calculates-a-hypothetical-result">How the tool calculates a hypothetical result</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Increase = the highest of prices, earnings and 2.5%. If two or three are equal highest, the result names each of them.</li>
    <li>New amount = amount before × (1 + increase ÷ 100).</li>
    <li>The new amount is rounded to the nearest 5p. An exact half rounds up.</li>
    <li>52-week equivalent = rounded weekly amount × 52.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The tool does not calculate past decisions. It reads them from the published record, because the figure used at the time can differ from the figure published now, and because some years had special rules. <a href="/sources-and-method/#models">Full method and limits</a>.</p>

  <script type="application/json" id="mechanism-data">{{ { years: history.years, checked: (history.checked_date | dateText) } | json | safe }}</script>
  <script type="module" src="/assets/js/tools/mechanism.js"></script>
</section>
